<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:05:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India news: Thousands of Indian pilgrims stranded in Saudi Arabia as Houthi attacks disrupt flights, government facilitating return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efe8670e295302be14abf210741393f5fb627e35c7061dc0978c98f4ab97b8ad</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:05:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T04:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-thousands-of-indian-pilgrims-stranded-in-saudi-arabia-as-houthi-attacks-disrupt-flights-g/live-79738437--d93f852ce517.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-thousands-of-indian-pilgrims-stranded-in-saudi-arabia-as-houthi-attacks-disrupt-flights-government-facilitating-return/live-79738437?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian pilgrims have been caught up in flight disruptions in Saudi Arabia amid escalating Houthi attacks. The government says it is working to arrange their return. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: Tens of thousands rally ahead of elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ec570eedb62bea7fa90387cdc94374563ed98da1c5d92eb2c0088f7dad012c2</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:05:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T03:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-tens-of-thousands-rally-ahead-of-elections/a-79738420--6d4a0cffd723.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-tens-of-thousands-rally-ahead-of-elections/a-79738420?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two years of student-led protests, Serbia will soon vote in what observers describe as a referendum-like snap election pitting strongman Aleksandar Vucic against the student movement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Airbnb scraps guest checkout chores such as cleaning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae52e9e3b915d2b41ffefbcad81d96692873eadc4c95505e7e9be4a0c4244a42</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:05:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T02:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airbnb-scraps-guest-checkout-chores-such-as-cleaning/a-79738340--615f4c6757d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airbnb-scraps-guest-checkout-chores-such-as-cleaning/a-79738340?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Under new rules, guests will no longer have to do tasks that cleaners would normally handle. Hosts can now only make "reasonable" requests, such as leaving dirty dishes in the sink and sorting trash from recycling.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tibet earthquake kills at least 16 people, injures dozens: state media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ce2dfdc2d51aff985ec78faec55c0f5035ae74ef50f38406a3c6d8aa11db0a3</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:05:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T23:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tibet-earthquake-kills-at-least-16-people-injures-dozens-state-media/a-79738117--804f662ec522.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tibet-earthquake-kills-at-least-16-people-injures-dozens-state-media/a-79738117?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A powerful magnitude 7 earthquake has struck Tibet in southwestern China, official media reported. Chinese state TV said it's the strongest quake to hit the remote Himalayan region in five years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Thousands protest for more abortion rights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2adb7129489642b81b3a01f7404e8897ee227ac253be393bd63e2b5bc83802fa</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:05:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T20:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-thousands-protest-for-more-abortion-rights/a-79737572--177050ad6205.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-thousands-protest-for-more-abortion-rights/a-79737572?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thousands rallied across Poland to demand abortion rights six years after a landmark court ruling tightened restrictions. The country has one of the strictest abortion rules in all of Europe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania's student protests are only getting bigger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e804467992f6984b816dfa87b3ee9a88317eec4428cbeb8fcd8e6b1d34f84f45</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T19:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-s-student-protests-are-only-getting-bigger/a-79735213--609bd8634d9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-s-student-protests-are-only-getting-bigger/a-79735213?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As police try to suppress anti-corruption protests by young Albanians, Prime Minister Edi Rama is claiming that "antifa" is behind the unrest. Few are buying that explanation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lina Attalah: Mada Masr journalist sent for trial in Egypt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65bd3beefa552923fa931257c7cd5127f5c3a0054e3319108de384bb7da13307</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T19:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lina-attalah-mada-masr-journalist-sent-for-trial-in-egypt/a-79736647--9d0c54466c32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lina-attalah-mada-masr-journalist-sent-for-trial-in-egypt/a-79736647?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lina Attalah, who is accused of managing a website without a license, will go to court next week. Mada Masr has published reporting critical of Egyptian President Abdel-Fattah el-Sissi's government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>96% of world's coral reefs face critical risk of collapse, IUCN warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:010c70cdd5f6c1322f0560d0e525f5515484ba7431446272260d8a1fedd6421e</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T18:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/96-of-world-s-coral-reefs-face-critical-risk-of-collapse-iucn-warns/a-79736234--5504c1b3916f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/96-of-world-s-coral-reefs-face-critical-risk-of-collapse-iucn-warns/a-79736234?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Almost all of the world’s shallow-water coral reefs are at risk of collapse by 2075, with climate change the biggest threat. A new study found that 96% of reef systems are critically endangered.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Mark Carney visits Turkey to boost trade ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ef471ee8507517998ccbebfea5e9774c9fdb58f58b9a4bba815aecf0dbbbbaf</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T17:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-s-mark-carney-visits-turkey-to-boost-trade-ties/a-79735039--dbd774d26d46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-s-mark-carney-visits-turkey-to-boost-trade-ties/a-79735039?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's the first bilateral visit by a Canadian prime minister to Turkey. Canada and Turkey upgraded their relations to a "strategic partnership" as Canada seeks to diversify trade beyond the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's Macron says 'illegitimate' protests will be banned in coming days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85411152dc6b8787a143da8b3e1c1cf4950968e30efcc6aab6fa19684f14dcac</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-macron-says-illegitimate-protests-will-be-banned-in-coming-days/a-79735137--c2dd52a04a07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-macron-says-illegitimate-protests-will-be-banned-in-coming-days/a-79735137?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron vowed to ban unauthorized protests after France was rocked by violence and looting. As anger over public services and the cost of living grows, authorities are bracing for more protests.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Are the French police the most violent in the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbd1acde3878edcb8bd7a54029c41bd208194680af74e928429f0ddd63495aa4</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-the-french-police-the-most-violent-in-the-eu/a-79732855--34f0b0f7045e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-the-french-police-the-most-violent-in-the-eu/a-79732855?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As protests continue in France, the French police are under scrutiny after new allegations of police brutality. The force has a bigger arsenal than most in Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran ready for another major US attack after midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40b54439aba9a3da3c8ed7d8a8ae5a5c5918097f66bae0e98150a91f7c8d38f6</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-ready-for-another-major-us-attack-after-midterm-elections/a-79734082--65d965ab6d67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-ready-for-another-major-us-attack-after-midterm-elections/a-79734082?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian officials say the goal is to keep the regime in power and threaten enough regional costs to make a prolonged campaign unattractive. US media reports indicate that Trump is considering strikes after the midterms.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is EU putting profits over human rights in Vietnam?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2ec2db9feb73f8a3bc41c3f22b39e495df27f7f1e6e7af59b16f7f78ad42ae9</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-eu-putting-profits-over-human-rights-in-vietnam/a-79732812--0a31793443b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-eu-putting-profits-over-human-rights-in-vietnam/a-79732812?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU and Vietnam are deepening economic and diplomatic ties, but closer cooperation raises concerns about whether Brussels is doing enough to address Hanoi's human rights record, labor standards and trade imbalances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Government expecting increased tax revenue in 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:656304364f4676baa8e48c9cbf829178bc7dcb1d91570e33ba09bfe2913f7cb9</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-government-expecting-increased-tax-revenue-in-2027/live-79728628--139a0de86753.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-government-expecting-increased-tax-revenue-in-2027/live-79728628?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finance Minister Lars Klingbeil said state tax revenue will increase by €4 billion in 2027. Meanwhile, public service websites have been coming back online after a PHP security scare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Gandhi's nephew forced to pull protest photos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:174635ff9c001574f852ce1076db6a9e4e39babc9ab65cb7e4647412fbf74481</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-s-nephew-forced-to-pull-protest-photos/live-79727462--8042d9d73860.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-s-nephew-forced-to-pull-protest-photos/live-79727462?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The requested removal of "objectionable" photos from a cultural center took place in state run by Modi's BJP.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France confirms first Shamonda virus infection in a human death of 'severely immunocompromised' individual</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d838dfa2e96eef0c442855cf9565df49a5956e9ba7f0a8d19061173b74738796</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-confirms-first-shamonda-virus-infection-in-a-human-death-of-severely-immunocompromised-indivi/a-79731991--31f7ca31d255.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-confirms-first-shamonda-virus-infection-in-a-human-death-of-severely-immunocompromised-individual/a-79731991?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Shamonda virus has been detected in a human for the first time, French health officials said. Authorities see no risk to the public, adding that the victim, who died in early October, was severely immunocompromised.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's Balochistan border region sees growing unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:468252726aa85416bbf3aced5639cd24ee469c21b0cc817eed8260616f3dbf69</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-balochistan-border-region-sees-growing-unrest/a-79716399--7cda0ee86ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-balochistan-border-region-sees-growing-unrest/a-79716399?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Violence is on the rise in Iran's border region with Afghanistan and Pakistan. The Iran war could shift the strategic balance for militant groups operating in the area.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Life near the front line in Sloviansk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:162b820e74d9542dec0787e85fce2aa6d04d882cae0585542aa17304c3fe84ed</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636--5ef08a6d884a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russian continues to attack Sloviansk in eastern Ukraine, thousands of residents refuse to leave or struggle to find a way out. For many, poverty, family ties and beloved pets make evacuation painfully difficult.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany arrests Ukrainian man suspected of spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0342456949908cbd37535ce6b842d913dcc13f694a021af89a3437986f1d6432</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-arrests-ukrainian-man-suspected-of-spying-for-russia/a-79732373--a3202cca0fcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-arrests-ukrainian-man-suspected-of-spying-for-russia/a-79732373?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The suspect is thought to have gathered defense-related information on the production of tanks and munitions, as well as details about NATO's eastern flank.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU's Sakharov Prize won by the International Criminal Court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:678070911f5604c10c5da9cd77347e9d810ae593ccdcad4ec01d3cc17ea17e5c</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-sakharov-prize-won-by-the-international-criminal-court/a-79730914--66e722beb7e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-sakharov-prize-won-by-the-international-criminal-court/a-79730914?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU has announced the International Criminal Court as the winner of this year's Sakharov Prize. The annual prize is awarded to individuals and organizations for their work in supporting human rights and democracy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Germany overhaul its economy before AfD grows stronger?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b257f40fcacf0dbc8c2ca096b677f7b58fd69f1077b3c3b2c8f7523e68355e59</id><updated>2026-10-23T05:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-overhaul-its-economy-before-afd-grows-stronger/a-79696102--b0df844ba99a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-overhaul-its-economy-before-afd-grows-stronger/a-79696102?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflicts, rising costs and Chinese competition are testing Germany's economic model like never before. Which new sectors could revive growth and contain the far-right AfD, whose support has grown larger than ever?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
